# netsurf: form named access -- an exact cheap pre-check before the control search (patch 322)
# Generated 2026-10-28
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 321)
#
# Patch 305 made a form's named controls shadow the whole prototype
# chain by wrapping every member of every prototype from
# HTMLFormElement.prototype up to Object.prototype, in place -- so
# Node.prototype.firstChild / nextSibling / parentNode / nodeType /
# ownerDocument and Element.prototype.getAttribute are wrapped for every
# node. On a non-form the wrapper is one isPrototypeOf. On a <form>
# every such read ran the full named-control search: controls() opens
# with querySelector('[form]') (an attribute selector, so the polyfill's
# JS walk over the whole document), then each listed control's owner
# walk, and on a miss formNamed scans every <img> with an owner walk
# each. Any DOM walk that passes a form paid that per member read, and
# the polyfill's own selector walk (jsQuery) reads several per element.
# theguardian.com/uk spent ~130 s of CPU in one QuickJS timer callback
# (a selector query from its client bundle) before a document appeared;
# the scorecard's 30 s run showed its title at 207 s. The document's
# named access (patch 288's layer above Document.prototype) had the same
# shape: every unknown document.x read ran an attribute-selector query.
#
#  - vita_polyfill.js: anyNamed(node, tags, n) -- can any element carry
#    the name n? getElementById(n), then a plain-selector query of the
#    nameable tags (the native matcher) with one getAttribute('name')
#    each. Exact: a name no element carries as id or name cannot shadow.
#    It runs under patch 297's inNamed guard (its own ownerDocument and
#    getAttribute reads on forms must not re-enter the lookups), and an
#    exception answers "maybe" (the full search runs, as before).
#  - controlsFirst (297/305's wrappers) and the layer above
#    HTMLFormElement.prototype return at once when anyNamed says no;
#    the layer above Document.prototype does the same for
#    form/img/embed/object/iframe. Numeric indexes keep their path.
#
# Measured: theguardian.com/uk in the simulator (run-live-sites, 30 s):
# 137.9 s user CPU, no document -> 3.6 s, document at 3.8 s. New gate page
# JS-form-walk-cost (FORMWALK 3/3): 20 attribute queries over ~2000
# elements with 3 forms and ~280 named images, 3695 ms before -> 286 ms;
# JS-form-named (FORMNAMED 7/7, patches 288/297/305) unchanged.
